6. Testing Documentation

A test-case table can be included:

Test Case	Input	Expected Result	Status
User Login	Valid credentials	Dashboard opens	Pass
User Login	Invalid credentials	Error message	Pass
Legal Search	Legal keyword	Relevant information displayed	Pass
AI Assistant	Legal question	General response displayed	Pass
Document Generator	Valid details	Document generated	Pass
Resource Search	Category selected	Relevant resources displayed	Pass
7. References and Sources

The documentation should list the sources used to develop the legal-information database, especially official government and legal-service sources.

Each legal-information entry should ideally record:

Source name
Source URL
Date accessed
Last updated date, where available
8. Project Documentation Deliverables

The final documentation package can contain:

Project report
Technical documentation
User manual
Database documentation
Testing report
Screenshots
Source-code documentation
References/bibliography
Future enhancement plan
9. Conclusion

The Project Documentation Phase creates a complete record of the Legalease project from initial idea to final implementation and testing. Good documentation makes the project easier to evaluate, use, maintain, update, and develop further. It also provides future developers with a clear understanding of how the system works.
